root[73]
├─0  heading[1]
│    │ depth: 1
│    └─0 text "The language contract"
├─1  paragraph[7]
│    ├─0 text "Ryo owns the concepts: the relations of the catalog. A language fulfils them. A language implements two\ntraits of "
│    ├─1 inlineCode "ryo::languages"
│    ├─2 text ", "
│    ├─3 inlineCode "Parse"
│    ├─4 text " and "
│    ├─5 inlineCode "Project"
│    └─6 text ", and that is all of ryo it implements: every relation of the\ncatalog is one required method of one of them, with no default body, so a relation added to the catalog is a\ncompile error in every language until the language has answered it. The crate does not compile with a relation\nleft out, and no engine code lists a language or a language's file names."
