│    ├─0 strong[1]
│    │   └─0 text "The shape rail."
│    ├─1 text " A language's walk or oracle compares the library's tree, mapped into the standard's vocabulary, with something independent of the code that built it: either an independent walk of the library's own tree ("
│    ├─2 inlineCode "fixtures/walk.rs"
│    ├─3 text "), or a projection of the standard itself (Python's comparison with "
│    ├─4 inlineCode "ast.dump"
│    └─5 text "). The conformance accepts either, so no language keeps a walk that compares the adapter with itself; a walk that stays only places the tokens."
